  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Ukraine - Support to Service Delivery in War-Affected Areas</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">This 18-month measure will provide equipment and assistance in response to urgent needs in the context of the evolving situation in the Ukrainian territories liberated from Russian military occupation. This will include assistance to the restoration of access to justice and the re-establishment of public safety and order, for example, by supporting the regional police offices, the prosecutor general, and other relevant authorities through the provision of equipment and flanking measures, such as relevant trainings, that act as enabler to their work. In addition, flexibility will be maintained to respond to other unforeseeable and urgent needs for the provision of basic services, including access to water and electricity in war affected areas, for example in situations such as the one created by the destruction of the Kakhovka dam, and access to information regarding the provision of services, where relevant. This shall also cover provision of equipment and assistance in response to urgent needs in the context of the intensified hybrid threat situation in neighbouring Moldova, as required.</narrative>
  </description>
